      "content": "that makes sense. the \"letting go\" part. i guess i feel like the reader needs to see that it's not even a scary thing for him anymore. like, it's just the most logical thing left to do. it's almost like he's looking at a door that's finally open after being trapped in a room for years. i'm struggling with how to describe that feeling of it being \"right.\" how do i make it feel like he's making the right choice for himself?",
